course: dictionary
lesson: 14507
title: Pending: waiting for the next step
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pending means waiting to be decided, done or finished. You will see it on screens and forms, such as «Your order is pending», which means the shop has not finished it yet. Read the words around it to find the clue: the order is not finished, so pending must mean still waiting.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Your order is still waiting to be finished» makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Pending can also describe a thing, as in «a pending decision», which is a decision not yet made.
explain: In formal language, pending can be a preposition that means until something happens. «The trip is cancelled pending further notice» means the trip stays cancelled until we hear more. Look for words like further notice, approval or a decision after pending: they often show the formal meaning.
fact: Pending means waiting to be decided, done or finished.
fact: Pending is an adjective when it describes something, as in «a pending decision».
fact: In formal language, pending can mean until something happens, as in «pending further notice».
fact: You often see pending on screens and forms, such as «payment pending».
fact: Useful phrases include «pending approval», «still pending» and «pending a decision».
exercise: «Your payment is pending.» What does pending mean here? | *Waiting to be finished | Free of charge | Already finished and gone | Written in bright ink
exercise: «The judge kept him in prison pending a decision.» What does pending mean in this sentence? | *Until a decision is made | Forever and always | Very quickly | Without any money
exercise: Which word could replace pending in «The result is still pending»? | Broken | Cheap | *Waiting | Loud
test: «Our class trip is cancelled pending further notice.» What does pending mean in this sentence? | *Until we hear more | Cancelled for ever | Very noisy | Already happened last week
test: «The form is pending approval.» Which phrase has the same meaning? | Given a prize | Approved long ago | *Waiting for approval | Torn in half
exam: In «The pending decision will be made today», what kind of word is pending? | *Adjective | Verb | Noun | Adverb
